  "explanation": "The original sources (D1S2, D1S6, D1S10, D1S13) explicitly state that Elisiv of Kyiv was married to Harald III, who is also identified as Harald Hardrada. Both names refer to the same individual and are supported by the text as valid answers for the spouse. Document D2 contains unrelated fictional content involving 'Lord Walker' and does not contradict the historical marriage described in D1. Therefore, both names from R5 are retained as distinct valid referents for the same person."
